# Local Postgres volume
.docker-data/

# drizzle-kit drift-check output — migrations are hand-authored under db/migrations
drizzle/

# TypeScript incremental build cache
*.tsbuildinfo

# Supabase CLI local state
supabase/.temp/

# Operational data lives outside the repo
/data/

# Local media store fallback when DATA_DIR is unset
.data/

# Offline basemap archives (PRD-13): operational data, built by scripts/construir-pmtiles.sh
# and copied here for local serving. Never versioned — can be tens of MB. See docs/mapas-offline.md
/public/mapa/*.pmtiles
# …except Chocó, committed deliberately and against the rule above (2026-08-21).
#
# The rule assumed ~50 MB per territory and a persistent volume to serve it from. Neither held:
# the real extract is 13 MB, and `DATA_DIR` on Railway is `/tmp/convite-data` — the container
# filesystem, with no volume mounted — so there is nowhere on the host for operational data to
# survive a deploy. Without this the offline map is inert in every environment, which makes
# PRD-13 a feature that exists only on the machine that built it.
#
# Revisit when a volume exists or a second territory lands: two or three of these in git history
# is a different conversation from one.
!/public/mapa/choco.pmtiles
